INT. LONDON TELEGRAPH OFFICE - NIGHT

Gas lamps hiss. Brass instruments click on a long oak counter. Rain streaks the high windows.

LADY CORDELIA ASHWORTH, 40s, black mourning silk, stands at the counter. She grips a folded paper so hard it crumples. Behind the counter, MISS PHILIPPA GRAY, 20s, the night clerk, ink on her fingers, watches her with wide eyes.

LADY CORDELIA
I must send it tonight.

MISS GRAY
The line to Calais is down, my lady.

LADY CORDELIA
Then send it by the northern route.

MISS GRAY
There's no northern route after ten.

She takes a step closer. She sets the paper on the counter. She does not let go of it.

LADY CORDELIA
My husband's creditors will be at my door by dawn.

MISS GRAY
I'm sorry for it.

She pulls the paper away. She reads it. Her face changes.

MISS GRAY (CONT'D)
This is addressed to a Mr. Hobb at the Admiralty.

LADY CORDELIA
It is.

The door opens. A gust of wet air. MR. ALISTAIR HOBB, 50s, stout, bowler hat, an umbrella dripping on the floorboards, steps inside. He sees them both and stops.

MR. HOBB
Lady Ashworth. I was told I might find you here.

LADY CORDELIA
By whom?

MR. HOBB
By him.

CONSTABLE JOSIAH DREW, 30s, blue coat, truncheon at his belt, enters behind him and shuts the door. He leans against it.

CONSTABLE DREW
Evening, ladies.

She steps back from the counter. She raises her chin. The clerk takes a half step behind the brass machines.

MISS GRAY
Constable, this is a public office.

CONSTABLE DREW
And that is a private telegram, miss.

He holds out a hand. She hesitates, then places the paper in it. He unfolds it and reads.

MR. HOBB
It names three of my colleagues.

LADY CORDELIA
It names the ones who took his money.

She turns away. She presses her fingers to her lips. The clerk watches her, then looks at the constable. He folds the telegram in half. He pockets it.

CONSTABLE DREW
There was no telegram.

MISS GRAY
There was not.

MR. HOBB
Constable, I must object--

CONSTABLE DREW
Mr. Hobb, it's raining. Go home.

He opens the door. Mr. Hobb stands very still, then jams his bowler on and goes out into the dark.
